  {
   "n": 7,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0",
   "html": "<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is/are correct?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "A MUX circuit can be used as a universal logic gate."
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "A MUX circuit can be designed using AND and OR gates."
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>\n\tA 2<em><sup>n</sup></em> input lines MUX has n-output lines.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "There is no feedback element present in a MUX."
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A",
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A, D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p>\n\t(a, d)<br />\n\tA 2<em><sup>n</sup></em> input lines MUX has n-select lines and only one output line.<br />\n\tAND, OR and NOT gates are required to design a MUX circuit.</p>"
  },
